      "page_number": 1,
      "text": "SYNTHETIC CAPSTONE CHALLENGE, Issue A\nAll procedures below are fictional.\n\nT1 光泽度 / Gloss — fictional ASTM D1627-16.\nConditioning stage: temprature 23 °C for 6 h（调节阶段）.\nMeasurement stage: observation angle 60°.\nMeasurement acceptance criterion: gloss 82–91 GU.\n\nT2 Scored-grid adhesion — fictional ISO 60038:2021.\nConditioning stage: 12 h at 24 °C.\nExecute these thermal-cycle stages in order: step 1 at -12 °C for 45 min; step 2 at 65 °C for 75 min.\nAfter-cycle acceptance criterion: adhesion class <=1."
    },
    {
      "page_number": 2,
      "text": "T3 Dry-film thickness — fictional ISO 60152:2025.\nMeasurement setup: clamp pre-load (the force applied by the specimen holder) 12 N.\nSpecimen material: Miralum-B (fictional material).\nRequired protective insert: QX-9 (fictional accessory).\nMeasurement acceptance criterion: film thickness 42–55 µm.\n\nT4 Colour difference — fictional ISO 60570:2025.\nConditioning stage: 31 °C for 90 min.\nMeasurement stage: D65 illuminant; compare with a master panel.\nMeasurement acceptance criterion: colour difference <=0.7 ΔE*ab.\nAcceptance thresholds describe the specimen; they do not guarantee a passing result."
    }
  ],
